WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.634
-Good evening, I'm Seth Meyers.
This is "Late Night."

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.100
We hope you're doing
well tonight.

00:00:04.100 --> 00:00:05.767
And now, if you don't mind,
we're going to get to the news.

00:00:05.767 --> 00:00:07.767
The White House
announced yesterday

00:00:07.767 --> 00:00:10.801
that President Biden
was interviewed over two days

00:00:10.801 --> 00:00:12.234
as part of the investigation

00:00:12.234 --> 00:00:14.300
into his handling
of classified documents.

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.133
It was supposed
to be one day,

00:00:16.133 --> 00:00:20.567
but, you know,
when you get that man talking.

00:00:20.567 --> 00:00:24.067
"Should we come back tomorrow
and wrap this up?"

00:00:24.067 --> 00:00:26.234
According to a new report,
White House staffers believe

00:00:26.234 --> 00:00:29.167
that President Biden's
handling of the war in Ukraine

00:00:29.167 --> 00:00:30.634
and the Hamas attack
on Israel

00:00:30.634 --> 00:00:31.901
could define his legacy.

00:00:31.901 --> 00:00:35.267
Said Biden, "Oh, good.
So not the bike thing?"

00:00:35.267 --> 00:00:37.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.868
Former President Trump
held a campaign

00:00:42.868 --> 00:00:44.200
rally last night
in New Hampshire

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:46.868
and blamed windmills
for killing whales.

00:00:46.868 --> 00:00:49.667
While normally when someone
says something like that,

00:00:49.667 --> 00:00:51.868
the next thing you see
is the backup quarterback

00:00:51.868 --> 00:00:54.167
warming up
on the sidelines.

00:00:54.167 --> 00:00:57.300
But nope, they're
leaving him in the game.

00:00:57.300 --> 00:00:59.567
House Republicans held
a closed door meeting yesterday

00:00:59.567 --> 00:01:01.334
to discuss the speakership,

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.834
and one member called it
"a therapy session,"

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:05.467
though if being locked
in a room

00:01:05.467 --> 00:01:08.334
with those people for two hours
feels like therapy,

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:12.234
you need to find
a new therapist.

00:01:12.234 --> 00:01:14.300
Robert F. Kennedy Jr.
announced yesterday

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.100
that he is dropping out
of the Democratic primary

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:19.267
and running for president
as an independent

00:01:19.267 --> 00:01:23.167
because, like his VAX card says,
he never had a shot.

00:01:23.167 --> 00:01:25.701
[ Laughter ]

00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:29.968
Yeah, yeah.

00:01:29.968 --> 00:01:31.200
No punches.

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:32.267
[ Applause ]

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:34.000
[ Laughs ]

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:36.000
A runner in the Chicago Marathon
over the weekend,

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:37.801
stopped when she saw
a stray kitten,

00:01:37.801 --> 00:01:39.767
but only so she could brag
to the kitten

00:01:39.767 --> 00:01:41.367
about running a marathon.

00:01:41.367 --> 00:01:43.534
[ Laughter ]

00:01:44.834 --> 00:01:47.734
Organizers for the
Los Angeles Olympics yesterday

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:50.200
proposed adding four new sports
to the games --

00:01:50.200 --> 00:01:54.167
lacrosse, squash, cricket
and driving to Santa Monica

00:01:54.167 --> 00:01:57.734
for a 4:00 p.m. audition
on a Friday.

00:01:57.734 --> 00:02:00.834
The jokes not for everyone,
but that is for our brothers

00:02:00.834 --> 00:02:03.300
and sisters in SAG-AFTRA
who are currently on strike.

00:02:03.300 --> 00:02:05.534
We wanted to write
a joke for them

00:02:05.534 --> 00:02:08.701
that hopefully they can enjoy...
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:08.701 --> 00:02:11.667
while we remain fingers
crossed and optimistic

00:02:11.667 --> 00:02:14.133
they will soon get
the deal they deserve

00:02:14.133 --> 00:02:18.067
In honor of the 20th anniversary
of the pumpkin spice latte,

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:21.267
Starbucks recently collaborated
with a fashion brand

00:02:21.267 --> 00:02:25.367
to offer a limited edition
Team PSL varsity jacket.

00:02:25.367 --> 00:02:28.467
Meanwhile, at Dunkin', they're
offering customers a shirt.

00:02:28.467 --> 00:02:30.567
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:32.167 --> 00:02:37.334
"I'm good, bro.
I'm good, bro."

00:02:37.334 --> 00:02:39.300
The shoe brand Crocs
recently unveiled

00:02:39.300 --> 00:02:41.868
its new limited edition
classic cowboy boot,

00:02:41.868 --> 00:02:44.334
which will go up
for sale later this month.

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:48.567
The boots will cost you $120
and all of your friends.

00:02:48.567 --> 00:02:50.901
[ Laughter ]

00:02:50.901 --> 00:02:54.000
And finally, a library director
in Alabama confirmed yesterday

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:56.167
that a children's picture
book was mistakenly

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:58.467
added to a list
of inappropriate titles

00:02:58.467 --> 00:03:00.901
because the author's
last name is gay.

00:03:00.901 --> 00:03:02.667
"Well, that explains a lot,"

00:03:02.667 --> 00:03:05.968
said recently Banned
YA author Dick Pervert.

00:03:05.968 --> 00:03:07.901
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.534 --> 00:03:12.234
That was a monologue,
everybody, we're off!

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:14.534
We're off and running.

00:03:14.534 --> 00:03:16.334
We got a great show
for you tonight.

00:03:16.334 --> 00:03:17.934
He's an Emmy-winning writer

00:03:17.934 --> 00:03:20.734
and an Emmy and Golden Globe
nominated actor.

00:03:20.734 --> 00:03:23.501
His children's book,
"Zilot &amp; Other

00:03:23.501 --> 00:03:24.701
Important Rhymes" is out now.

00:03:24.701 --> 00:03:26.767
Bob Odenkirk is back
on the show, everybody.

00:03:26.767 --> 00:03:29.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:29.300 --> 00:03:32.300
He is just about to start
his second season

00:03:32.300 --> 00:03:34.501
as a cast member
at "Saturday Night Live."

00:03:34.501 --> 00:03:36.567
Shoemaker, you remember my
second year

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:38.100
at "Saturday Night Live?"

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.367
His is going to go a lot better,

00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.133
which is insane and frankly,
unfair.

00:03:42.133 --> 00:03:44.100
He's wonderful.
Marcello Hernandez

00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.334
is also going to be joining us.

00:03:46.334 --> 00:03:47.834
And she -- we're so happy
to have her here.

00:03:47.834 --> 00:03:49.834
She was a writer here
at this very show.

00:03:49.834 --> 00:03:51.234
She's an incredible
comedian.

00:03:51.234 --> 00:03:53.067
Her new book,
"Unreliable Narrator:

00:03:53.067 --> 00:03:55.934
Me, Myself and Imposter
Syndrome" is out now.

00:03:55.934 --> 00:03:58.601
Our friend Aparna Nancherla
is back with us,

00:03:58.601 --> 00:04:01.100
so excited to talk to her.

00:04:01.100 --> 00:04:03.434
Also real quick,
during the strike,

00:04:03.434 --> 00:04:05.033
I started a podcast
with my brother.

00:04:05.033 --> 00:04:06.167
It's called "Family Trips,"

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.200
and we talked to a different
celebrity guests

00:04:08.200 --> 00:04:09.701
about the trips
they took as kids.

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:11.767
We just recorded ones
with John Mulaney

00:04:11.767 --> 00:04:13.701
and Nick Offerman this week.
They'll be out soon.

00:04:13.701 --> 00:04:15.467
And, you know,
I've been saying every time

00:04:15.467 --> 00:04:17.100
I hold up this picture
that I'm the cute one

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:18.667
and my brother
is the ugly one.

00:04:18.667 --> 00:04:20.968
And a lot of people
don't like that joke,

00:04:20.968 --> 00:04:21.968
but it's not a joke.

00:04:21.968 --> 00:04:23.133
He's the ugly one.

00:04:23.133 --> 00:04:25.234
[ Laughter ]

00:04:26.968 --> 00:04:28.567
And I have to say that
because I want you to know

00:04:28.567 --> 00:04:30.234
there's a podcast
where you can go for the truth.

00:04:30.234 --> 00:04:32.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:32.267 --> 00:04:34.234
Well, you guys,
yesterday the Writers Guild

00:04:34.234 --> 00:04:37.300
voted to ratify a new contract
with the studios,

00:04:37.300 --> 00:04:39.634
bringing an end to the five
months long writers strike.

00:04:39.634 --> 00:04:42.133
We've been back at work for a
few days, but now it's official.

00:04:42.133 --> 00:04:44.400
And after a long summer
of picketing and chanting,

00:04:44.400 --> 00:04:45.868
it makes sense
that they're exhausted.

00:04:45.868 --> 00:04:47.267
And writing jokes is hard work.

00:04:47.267 --> 00:04:49.701
They have to write hundreds,
hundreds of jokes every day

00:04:49.701 --> 00:04:51.501
just to get the 10 or 12
we use in the monologue.

00:04:51.501 --> 00:04:55.334
And honestly, a lot of the jokes
they write just aren't good.

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:56.968
[ Laughter ]

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:59.467
And sometimes I think they throw
in a few stinkers on purpose

00:04:59.467 --> 00:05:01.267
just to fill the page
and meet the assignment.

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:04.033
But just because
we support labor movements,

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:05.734
that doesn't mean
we can tolerate laziness,

00:05:05.734 --> 00:05:07.167
which means it's time
for another

00:05:07.167 --> 00:05:08.467
"Surprise Inspection."

00:05:08.467 --> 00:05:10.434
[ Bugle call ]

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:15.467
♪♪

00:05:15.467 --> 00:05:16.501
So, here's how this works.

00:05:16.501 --> 00:05:18.767
I'm going to read
some real jokes

00:05:18.767 --> 00:05:21.501
that were really submitted
by my writers,

00:05:21.501 --> 00:05:25.734
paid writers, paid better
than ever before...

00:05:25.734 --> 00:05:28.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:31.601 --> 00:05:33.200
...that are unusable
for the show.

00:05:33.200 --> 00:05:36.033
Some are dumb, some are
offensive,

00:05:36.033 --> 00:05:37.467
some are just insane.

00:05:37.467 --> 00:05:39.367
Most importantly, the writers
don't know we're doing this.

00:05:39.367 --> 00:05:41.334
And because a lot of them
don't watch the show,

00:05:41.334 --> 00:05:43.701
they'll never know.

00:05:43.701 --> 00:05:45.267
So let's get started.

00:05:45.267 --> 00:05:48.634
It was announced last week that
Usher will headline next year's

00:05:48.634 --> 00:05:50.200
Super Bowl halftime show.

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:53.133
Okay, but who will help
everyone find their seats?

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:55.834
[ Light laughter ]

00:05:55.834 --> 00:05:58.167
[ Applause ]

00:06:00.200 --> 00:06:02.267
Matt wrote that joke.

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:06.801
And he was -- he was unaware

00:06:06.801 --> 00:06:09.000
we were doing something
called "Surprise Inspection"

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:12.567
when he took the photo.
That's why he's smiling.

00:06:12.567 --> 00:06:15.434
According to the personal
finance website WalletHub,

00:06:15.434 --> 00:06:18.634
Orlando is the best foodie city
in the country.

00:06:18.634 --> 00:06:22.634
Guys, it's expensive,
but it's so worth it.

00:06:22.634 --> 00:06:24.767
[ Light laughter ]

00:06:26.868 --> 00:06:28.300
Mike Scollins wrote that joke.

00:06:28.300 --> 00:06:33.033
Mike Scollins is what's
known as a bad guy.

00:06:33.033 --> 00:06:34.434
He's a bad guy who writes jokes

00:06:34.434 --> 00:06:36.834
that don't make people laugh
or make them happy.

00:06:36.834 --> 00:06:39.000
It makes them think,
Oh, my God, they are eating...

00:06:39.000 --> 00:06:41.901
[ Laughter ]

00:06:41.901 --> 00:06:43.067
...they're eating Shamu.

00:06:43.067 --> 00:06:45.400
That's the kind of joke.

00:06:45.400 --> 00:06:47.434
But, you know, let's not forget,
going back

00:06:47.434 --> 00:06:48.801
to Goldich's jokes,

00:06:48.801 --> 00:06:51.067
there's not ushers
at football games.

00:06:51.067 --> 00:06:53.234
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.033 --> 00:06:59.234
How did they find their seats?

00:06:59.234 --> 00:07:00.834
The [bleep] ticket number.

00:07:00.834 --> 00:07:04.133
[ Laughter ]

00:07:04.133 --> 00:07:05.300
Also Usher.

00:07:05.300 --> 00:07:07.901
So there's one usher
for the whole...?

00:07:07.901 --> 00:07:11.067
One guy running around?

00:07:11.067 --> 00:07:14.033
Today was musician
Sting's 72nd birthday.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.734
And while he started
his party today,

00:07:15.734 --> 00:07:17.868
he probably won't finish
till tomorrow.

00:07:17.868 --> 00:07:20.400
[ Light laughter ]

00:07:20.400 --> 00:07:23.667
Now, that joke is dependent
on you

00:07:23.667 --> 00:07:26.734
knowing that
Sting practices tantric sex.

00:07:26.734 --> 00:07:28.767
[ Laughter ]

00:07:28.767 --> 00:07:31.467
[ Coughs ]

00:07:31.467 --> 00:07:33.234
Obviously, guys, you guys
don't know that.

00:07:33.234 --> 00:07:35.934
It's literally
all Ally talks about.

00:07:35.934 --> 00:07:37.968
[ Laughter ]

00:07:39.501 --> 00:07:42.567
We stopped playing
sting music in the office

00:07:42.567 --> 00:07:43.934
because if you do,
she just is like,

00:07:43.934 --> 00:07:47.400
"Do you guys know?"
And we're like, "Alright."

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:50.067
[ Coughs ]
Excuse me, guys.

00:07:50.067 --> 00:07:51.868
I cough when things
are going really well.

00:07:51.868 --> 00:07:54.300
[ Laughter ]

00:07:56.934 --> 00:07:59.968
Eggo has released
a new maple syrup flavored milk,

00:07:59.968 --> 00:08:02.567
or, as it's known in Canada,
breast milk.

00:08:02.567 --> 00:08:06.601
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.601 --> 00:08:09.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:15.634 --> 00:08:17.634
Yeah, it's that dude.

00:08:17.634 --> 00:08:19.067
Authorities in Indianapolis

00:08:19.067 --> 00:08:21.367
recently captured
an escaped pet monkey

00:08:21.367 --> 00:08:23.834
that was spotted drinking
a beer out of a garbage can.

00:08:23.834 --> 00:08:26.667
The monkey's name is
Slurious George.

00:08:29.067 --> 00:08:31.467
Ian wrote that joke,

00:08:31.467 --> 00:08:33.734
and that's the face he makes
when he writes one.

00:08:33.734 --> 00:08:35.868
[ Laughter ]

00:08:37.934 --> 00:08:39.534
"Do you get it?

00:08:42.834 --> 00:08:45.000
It's based on Curious George."
"Yeah, I get it."

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.467
[ Light laughter ]

00:08:47.467 --> 00:08:50.000
-That's -- this next one's
an Ian joke as well,

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:53.400
and I'm confident

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.100
you're going to think
Slurious George

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.400
is the best of his work.

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:58.501
[ Laughter ]

00:08:58.501 --> 00:09:03.400
We're going to all long
for Slurious George in a moment.

00:09:03.400 --> 00:09:04.934
Florida wildlife officials

00:09:04.934 --> 00:09:07.033
were recently called
to a yacht club

00:09:07.033 --> 00:09:09.834
after a bear was spotted
on a docked sailboat.

00:09:09.834 --> 00:09:12.834
Officials gave the bear
a stern talking to

00:09:12.834 --> 00:09:14.734
and then another one on the bow.

00:09:14.734 --> 00:09:16.868
[ Audience groans ]

00:09:16.868 --> 00:09:22.968
-So -- so a [bleep] bear

00:09:22.968 --> 00:09:27.767
was on a boat,
and Ian's take on that

00:09:27.767 --> 00:09:32.801
was not to make a joke
about the bear part,

00:09:32.801 --> 00:09:38.133
but just that there's a bow
and a stern on a boat.

00:09:38.133 --> 00:09:40.467
A bear.

00:09:40.467 --> 00:09:43.467
A bear was on a boat.

00:09:43.467 --> 00:09:47.601
He didn't think
there would be a joke in that.

00:09:47.601 --> 00:09:49.767
I know exactly how it happened.

00:09:49.767 --> 00:09:51.901
He was like --
We'll show him.

00:09:51.901 --> 00:09:54.567
[ Laughter ]

00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:00.300
[ Laughter ]

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:01.968
Cheese delivery service
in Florida

00:10:01.968 --> 00:10:03.601
recently set
the Guinness World Record

00:10:03.601 --> 00:10:05.834
for world's largest
charcuterie board.

00:10:05.834 --> 00:10:09.267
And then to celebrate,
they threw a huge party.

00:10:09.267 --> 00:10:12.434
[ Light laughter ]

00:10:12.434 --> 00:10:15.734
[ Light applause ]

00:10:15.734 --> 00:10:17.934
Alright, you know what?
You got six claps.

00:10:17.934 --> 00:10:19.200
Let's see who it was.

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:20.467
Yeah.

00:10:20.467 --> 00:10:22.033
[ Laughter ]

00:10:22.033 --> 00:10:25.067
[ Applause ]

00:10:25.067 --> 00:10:28.868
You're off a roll!

00:10:28.868 --> 00:10:30.901
Customs officials
at a Minnesota airport

00:10:30.901 --> 00:10:33.033
recently confiscated
a box of giraffe poop

00:10:33.033 --> 00:10:34.467
from an international traveler.

00:10:34.467 --> 00:10:37.300
Apparently, she tried to bring
it into the duty-free shop.

00:10:37.300 --> 00:10:40.601
[ Laughter ]

00:10:40.601 --> 00:10:42.234
That's Brian, everybody.

00:10:42.234 --> 00:10:44.667
And would you believe,
this is going to shock you,

00:10:44.667 --> 00:10:47.267
his best friend
on staff is Ian?

00:10:47.267 --> 00:10:49.467
[ Laughter ]

00:10:50.601 --> 00:10:54.334
A truck in Ontario, Canada --
a truck in Ontario, Canada

00:10:54.334 --> 00:10:57.167
yesterday spilled a load of
produce across the highway.

00:10:57.167 --> 00:10:58.734
Said the driver, "Oh, no.

00:10:58.734 --> 00:11:00.901
They're going
to garnish my celery."

00:11:00.901 --> 00:11:03.300
[ Light laughter ]

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:10.868
So they went on strike.
They walked around.

00:11:10.868 --> 00:11:12.734
They walked around
buildings like this one.

00:11:12.734 --> 00:11:15.234
Like, "What are you
going to do without us?"

00:11:15.234 --> 00:11:17.634
[ Laughter ]

00:11:20.467 --> 00:11:23.601
That was Brian again.

00:11:23.601 --> 00:11:26.200
We make him and Ian
share a desk.

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:28.000
[ Laughter ]

00:11:28.000 --> 00:11:30.467
Princess Kate Middleton
participated last week

00:11:30.467 --> 00:11:31.901
in a wheelchair rugby game.

00:11:31.901 --> 00:11:33.434
"Ah, it wasn't for real?,"

00:11:33.434 --> 00:11:34.834
asked Meghan.

00:11:34.834 --> 00:11:37.000
[ Audience "oohs" ]

00:11:37.000 --> 00:11:39.934
[ Laughter ]

00:11:39.934 --> 00:11:43.300
If you've been paying attention,
you know that's this guy.

00:11:43.300 --> 00:11:45.667
[ Laughter ]

00:11:46.634 --> 00:11:48.968
The deputy mayor of Paris
last week

00:11:48.968 --> 00:11:51.767
addressed the widespread
rise of bedbugs across the city

00:11:51.767 --> 00:11:53.734
and said, "No one is safe."

00:11:53.734 --> 00:11:56.501
So before asking someone
voulez-vous

00:11:56.501 --> 00:11:59.801
coucher avec moi,
ask yourself

00:11:59.801 --> 00:12:02.167
itchy, itchy, ya-ya, da-da.

00:12:02.167 --> 00:12:03.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:03.367 --> 00:12:05.534
Okay.
Credit where credit is due.

00:12:05.534 --> 00:12:06.868
Congratulations, Matt.

00:12:06.868 --> 00:12:08.734
You earned your smile, buddy.

00:12:08.734 --> 00:12:11.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:12.234 --> 00:12:14.100
[ Laughs ]

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:16.167
I would not have guessed
that that was --

00:12:16.167 --> 00:12:18.767
that was going to be
our heavy hitter.

00:12:18.767 --> 00:12:21.100
In honor of Halloween,
Burger King has reintroduced

00:12:21.100 --> 00:12:24.067
a whopper with an orange bun
and black sesame seeds

00:12:24.067 --> 00:12:25.434
while McDonald's is celebrating

00:12:25.434 --> 00:12:27.601
by leaving the corpses
in the ball pit.

00:12:27.601 --> 00:12:29.834
[ Laughter ]

00:12:33.167 --> 00:12:34.634
[ Laughter ]

00:12:34.634 --> 00:12:37.100
He was our strike captain.

00:12:37.100 --> 00:12:38.968
He was out there
every day this summer.

00:12:38.968 --> 00:12:40.801
And let me just say,
as our strike captain,

00:12:40.801 --> 00:12:42.434
you did a fantastic job, buddy.

00:12:42.434 --> 00:12:44.033
Congratulations
in everything you did.

00:12:44.033 --> 00:12:45.467
Thank you for getting us out,

00:12:45.467 --> 00:12:47.501
getting the writing staff of
this show out there every day.

00:12:47.501 --> 00:12:49.334
And it is wonderful
to have them all back.

00:12:49.334 --> 00:12:51.501
And look, they can't
all be fastballs,

00:12:51.501 --> 00:12:54.968
but it is great to have this
writing staff back with us.

00:12:54.968 --> 00:12:56.968
This has been
"Surprise Inspection."

00:12:56.968 --> 00:12:58.868
[ Bugle call ]

00:12:58.868 --> 00:13:01.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.367
♪♪

